# Buildroot makeusers table for lemnosd.service (the Raze device package
# imports Lemnos's lemnosd layer). The image root is a read-only EROFS slot,
# where systemd-sysusers cannot add users at boot, so the `lemnos` user that
# Lemnos's sysusers entry describes (packaging/systemd/lemnos.sysusers,
# installed as /usr/lib/sysusers.d/lemnos.conf) is created at build time with
# the same groups: i2c, gpio and video own the device nodes lemnosd opens.
# HeliOS services that talk to lemnosd join the `lemnos` group
# (SupplementaryGroups=lemnos), which owns /run/lemnos/lemnosd.sock.
# Columns: username uid group gid password home shell groups comment (see
# Buildroot's makeusers).
lemnos -1 lemnos -1 * /run/lemnos /bin/false i2c,gpio,video Lemnos hardware service
